Tell the HarmonyOS input method what a field is for.

The system keyboard offers a user-name keyboard, a new-password keyboard with
strong-password suggestions, and one-time-code autofill, and Password Vault
only offers to fill or save when it sees a user-name field and a password
field. The web states this with autocomplete tokens, which no TextInputType
carries. On OHOS, InputMethodController::TextInputFlags() adds three bits for
username, new-password and one-time-code, above the shared flags. The OHOS
input method (overlay) maps them to IME_TEXT_INPUT_TYPE_USER_NAME,
NEW_PASSWORD and ONE_TIME_CODE.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

